==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
This stage's first outbreak can be particularly easy, as the Zapy does insignificant single target damage with warp, which can easily be countered with proper stallers (e.g. [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] or [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]]). The rest of the stage can be easily be done using the strategy for the non-outbreak version, as the only change besides Zapy is Zackie Pengs, which can easily be dealt with using anti-Zombie attackers or high damage, stackable attackers.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
-

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The Maawth can be stalled fairly easily with [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] to rack up cash. Once the Zackie Peng arrives, take it down using a [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] such as [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]]. Once Zackie Peng is dealt with, you should have no problem stalling for a maxed wallet.

The combination of Commander Ostromeda and Corporal Weylands ensure any non-Warp Immune units will be pushed back relentlessly, losing you ground bit by bit. Due to this, the ideal meatshield here is Catellite (or Soap Cat if paired with [[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]]) due to their high health and Immunity to Warp. It is worth noting that at at level 54 Catellite can survive 3 Ostromeda hits with a Defense Up (Sm) [[Cat Combo]], and at level 60+ can do the same without the need for any Combos. For attackers, anything that outranges Ostromeda will do fine; however, keep in mind that any units with a long foreswing will be interrupted by Warp more often.

The Formicidaean Ariants are unlikely to be a threat, as Ostromeda's constant pushing will make them miss their attacks.

